# R/02_application

Empirical application of the three ETAS estimators to a real earthquake
catalogue.

This folder contains the script that fits ETAS, ETAS-FLP, and ETAS-P to
the Italian earthquake catalogue `catalog.withcov`, distributed with the
`etasFLP` R package, using distance to the nearest mapped fault as a
spatial covariate in both the triggering and (for ETAS-P) the background
component.

## Files

- **`studio_simulazione_etas_parametrico.R`**
  Fits the three models with `magn.threshold = 2.5` (the completeness
  threshold used throughout the main analysis) and
  `magn.threshold.back = 3.9`. Produces Table 2 (estimated ETAS
  parameters) and Table 3 (background component summary) of the main
  text, and Figures 7–8 (spatial distribution of the catalogue and
  fitted intensities).

## Note

This script depends only on the `etasclass()`/`etasclass.par()`
definitions in `R/01_core_estimation/etas_parametric_final_plan_no_smooth.R`
and on the `catalog.withcov` dataset bundled with `etasFLP`; it does not
require any of the simulation outputs from `01_core_estimation`.
